1. Title: SQL Injection Exploitation Report

SQL Injection Exploitation on a Deliberately Vulnerable Web Application
2. Introduction
SQL Injection (SQL) is a web application vulnerability that occurs when user-supplied input is incorrectly included in an SQL query. An attacker may manipulate the SQL statement to bypass authentication or retrieve information from a database.
This practical was performed in an authorized and controlled laboratory environment using a deliberately vulnerable web application. The purpose was to understand how SQL Injection works, demonstrate its impact, and identify methods for preventing the vulnerability.
3. Objectives
The objectives of this practical were to:
* Identify a SQL Injection vulnerability
* Demonstrate SQL Injection in the laboratory application.
* Understand how the SQL query is manipulated.
* Explain the security impact of SQL Injection.
